    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1005">

                <pb facs="0928" n="838" sameAs="frus:frus1918Russiav02/pg838"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 860d.00/300</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Chargé in Sweden</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Whitehouse</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1918-10-16T17:00:00-04:00"><hi rendition="#italic">October 16,
                                1918, 5 p.m.</hi></date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1215. Your 2985, October 12, 5 p.m. While fears for the consequences which would
                    follow withdrawal of enemy troops may be well founded, at the same time in
                    investigating and reporting further on this question, bear in mind that
                    Department has confidential information to show that Germany is instigating
                    requests for protection by German troops on the same pretexts.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                            >Lansing</hi></signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
